            """Args:
                id: Unique identifier of the object; other nodes refer to it by this id.
                primitive: Kind of object: built-in solid (sphere, box, plane, cylinder, cone, torus, capsule), extruded path or text, imported mesh, clay, map, globe, volume, voxels, parametric surface or heightfield. Required.
                material: Id of the material the object is drawn with; on an imported mesh it replaces every imported material. A voxels object uses it only for palette entries that name none, and a volume ignores it.
                resolution: Cells along the longest side of a clay object's bounds, and along the longer side of a map ground's grid; 8 to 256, default 64.
                fingerprints: Amount, 0 to 1, of fingerprint-like surface roughness on a clay object; 0 (default) is smooth.
                boil: Times per second the clay roughness pattern is re-seeded, so it shimmers in steps; 0 (default) never changes it. Has no visible effect while fingerprints is 0.
                seed: Seed of the clay roughness pattern; absent, it is derived from the object id.
                mesh: Id of the mesh or mesh-sequence asset to draw; required when primitive is mesh.
                text: Text to draw as a solid when primitive is text; the element's text content, when present, takes precedence.
                font: Font family used for primitive text; under project fontPolicy pinned it must be the family of a font asset.
                node: With primitive="mesh" and an imported model: draw only the node of that name and its descendants, placed so that the node's own origin is the object's origin (the node's transform within the model is dropped, the transforms below it are kept). The first node of that name in the model's node order is used.
                materialOverride: With primitive="mesh" and an imported model: a space-separated list of imported-material-name:document-material-id pairs. Each primitive of the model whose material has that name is drawn with the document material instead. A material with no pair keeps its imported look. @material, when present, replaces every material and takes precedence.
                tracking: Extra space after every character of primitive="text", in thousandths of an em of the text size (the object's height). Negative values tighten. Valid only with primitive="text".
                path: Path data of the outline to extrude when primitive is extrude; required there.
                depth: Thickness in scene units of a box or of an extruded shape (centred on the origin along z); default 10.
                bevel: Width in scene units of the chamfer on both faces of extruded text or paths, limited to half the depth; default 0.
                width: Width in scene units of a box or plane; absent, twice the radius.
                height: Height in scene units of a box, plane, cylinder, cone or capsule (default twice the radius; capsule four times), the tube diameter of a torus (default 0.7 of the radius), and the text size (default 100).
                segments: Tessellation count of round shapes, 3 to 512 (default 32); a globe never uses fewer than 24. For a plane, the grid is segments by segments quads, 1 to 1024.
                x: Position along x in scene units, in the parent frame; default 0.
                y: Position along y in scene units, in the parent frame; default 0.
                z: Position along z in scene units, in the parent frame; default 0.
                rotation: Rotation in degrees about the z axis, default 0. The object is turned about x first, then y, then z (matrix Rz*Ry*Rx), all about the parent's axes.
                rotationX: Rotation in degrees about the x axis, default 0. Applied first: the object is turned about x, then y (rotationY), then z (rotation), all about the parent's axes.
                rotationY: Rotation in degrees about the y axis, default 0. Applied second: after rotationX and before rotation (z), all about the parent's axes.
                scaleX: Scale factor along the x axis; default 1.
                scaleY: Scale factor along the y axis; default 1.
                scaleZ: Scale factor along the z axis; default 1.
                radius: Radius in scene units of a sphere, cylinder, cone, capsule or torus ring; unset width and height are derived from it (twice the radius for a box or plane). Default 50.
                castShadow: Whether the object casts shadows; default true. An object that is a shadow catcher never casts one.
                receiveShadow: Whether the object receives shadows; default true.
                shadowCatcher: The surface draws no colour of its own. It is transparent where no light is blocked and black, with alpha up to @opacity, where the shadow casters block the light that would reach it, so that it darkens what is behind the 3D layer by the share of light that is taken away (ambient light counted). It does not cast shadows.
                visible: Whether the object is drawn; default true.
                opacity: Opacity from 0 (invisible) to 1 (opaque), multiplied with that of its parents; default 1.
                start: Time in seconds, on the parent's timeline, at which the object appears; it is also zero of the object's own time. A transition into it can make it appear earlier. Default 0.
                end: Time in seconds, on the parent's timeline, at which the object disappears (exclusive); a transition out of it keeps it shown until the transition ends. Without end or such a transition, it stays until its parent ends.
                condition: Expression evaluated over time; the object is drawn only while it is true.
                parent: Id of another node, camera or light whose world transform this object follows; position, angles and scales are then in that frame. A 2D parent contributes its 2D world transform.
                parentJoint: With a @parent (or a transformConstraint of type="parent") that is an object3D drawing an imported model: the name of a node of that model. The element is placed in that node's frame as the model's clips pose it, instead of in the object's own frame. The first node of that name in the model's node order is used.
                motionBlur: Motion blur: on, off, or inherit (default) the setting of the parent, else the project. Consecutive 3D objects sharing a parent are drawn as one pass, blurred by the first one's setting.
                animationClip: Name or index of the animation clip of an imported model to play, looped over its duration.
                animationSpeed: Speed multiplier of the object's source time (model clip, mesh sequence, numbered volume sequence, pyro): source time is object time times this plus animationOffset. Default 1.
                animationOffset: Seconds added to the object's source time (model clip, mesh sequence, numbered volume sequence, pyro) after the speed multiplier; default 0.
                animationClipTo: With primitive="mesh" and an imported model: a second clip (by name or index, as @animationClip) the model is blended toward by @animationBlend. It plays at the object's time scaled by @animationSpeed plus @animationOffsetTo.
                animationBlend: Weight of @animationClipTo, 0 to 1 (animatable): 0 is @animationClip alone, 1 is @animationClipTo alone, between them translation, scale and morph weights blend linearly and rotation along the shortest arc. A node a clip does not animate keeps its rest pose in that clip. Without @animationClipTo the weight blends toward the rest pose.
                animationOffsetTo: Seconds added to the time of the second clip (animationClipTo) that is blended in; default 0.
                morphWeights: Weights of the imported model morph targets in order, replacing the clip weights; named morph children override single targets.
                materialVariant: Name of the material variant of the imported model to draw; an unknown name keeps the default material, and a set material replaces it.
                instances: Number of copies of the object drawn (default 1); each is evaluated with its own index and count.
                map: primitive="map": the map asset as ground in the object's xy plane, one map pixel per scene unit, draped with the map as drawn; @terrain (tiles of elevation, Terrarium or Mapbox Terrain-RGB per @terrainEncoding) raises it toward the camera (−z) by true height times @exaggeration on a grid of @resolution cells, and @buildings extrudes the footprints of its first basemap's vector tiles to their heights. Terrain and buildings need a Web Mercator map. primitive="globe": a sphere of @radius and @segments (poles on the y axis, 0° longitude facing the camera) draped with the map's content drawn over the whole world. @material dresses the ground, the globe and the buildings. @textureSize is the drape's resolution in pixels along a map's longer side, and a globe drape's height (its width is twice that); it does not change what the drape shows.
                terrain: Id of the tiles asset with elevation data that raises a map ground or relieves a globe.
                terrainEncoding: How elevation is encoded in terrain tiles: terrarium (default) or mapbox.
                exaggeration: Multiplier of terrain heights on a map or globe, and of building heights on a map; 1 (default) is true scale, 0 flattens.
                buildings: On a map, extrudes the building footprints of the first basemap's vector tiles to their heights (8 m when a footprint has none); default false.
                textureSize: Resolution in pixels of the drape texture: its longer side on a map, its height on a globe (width twice that, height capped at 4096); 64 to 8192, default 2048.
                planetRadius: Version 1.3 globe relief: physical datum radius in metres. Radial scene displacement is elevationMetres * radius / planetRadius * exaggeration. Flat map terrain keeps its existing scale.
                terrainTileSize: Width and height in pixels of the terrain tiles, which must match the tiles in the asset; a power of two up to 4096, default 256. Only on a globe with terrain.
                terrainZoom: Zoom level, 0 to 22, of the terrain tiles read for a globe; absent, derived from the segments and tile size within the archive's zoom range. Only on a globe with terrain.
                terrainMissing: What a missing terrain tile does on a globe: error (default) fails, zero treats its elevation as 0. Only on a globe with terrain.
                terrainMemoryMiB: Upper bound in MiB, 1 to 4096 (default 128), for the memory of globe terrain (surface and tile cache). Only on a globe with terrain.
                voxels: Version 1.3. With primitive="voxels" (VOX4): the voxelAsset whose cells this object is made of. Position, scale and the other transform attributes are those of every object3D; the origin of the cells is the corner of the bounding box of the occupied cells.
                cellSize: Only with primitive="voxels" (VOX5): scene units a cell. Absent, the voxelAsset's own cellSize if it has one, else the cell size that an srvol asset's grid says, else 1.
                palette: Only with primitive="voxels" (VOX5): the token `file` (the colours of the file, which needs a file that has them) or the materials, as IDs separated by spaces, of the palette indices 1, 2, ... in order, at most 255 (VOX6). The material of a cell is the one of its index, else the object's own `material`, else the colour of the file; an index with none of the three is an error that names it. Absent, `file` if the file has colours and otherwise the object's `material`.
                surface: Only with primitive="voxels" (VOX5): `blocks`, the only value so far, draws every exposed face of a cell as a quad. The engine's default is `blocks`; it is not an XSD default so that it can be refused on any other primitive.
                surfaceMemoryMiB: Only with primitive="voxels" (VOX5): the most memory, in MiB, that the surface of the cells may take while it is made and drawn (1,240 bytes for each quad at the peak: its compact form, the builder's vertices and indices, the copy a mesh upload keeps and the buffers on the device). The engine's default is 128; it is not an XSD default so that it can be refused on any other primitive. A surface over it is an error that names the cause, never a surface cut short.
                volume: Id of the volume asset to draw when primitive is volume; a volume object needs exactly one of this and a pyro child.
            """
            ...

