            """Each frame, the stateful nodes inside start from their zero state and advance @steps steps (fewer with until="converged") before the frame is drawn. For stills; SREP 68 is the animated form.

            Args:
                tags: Space-separated free-form labels on the node. With safeArea enforcement on, a node tagged cta or logo is checked to stay inside the safe region unless safeAreaForce exempts it.
                safeAreaForce: true exempts this node and everything it contains (for a symbol: every instance of it, and what it draws) from the safeArea enforce check (SA01); validate lists every node that carries it (SA02), so a deliberate placement outside the safe region is never silent.
                z: Stacking order among siblings: nodes with a higher integer draw above lower ones; 0 when absent. Not used for stacking by 3D objects, 3D particle nodes, ocean nodes and cameras.
                visible: When false, the node and everything it contains are not drawn; true when absent.
                opacity: Node opacity from 0 (transparent) to 1 (opaque), multiplied with the opacity of its ancestors; 1 when absent.
                start: Time in seconds, on the parent's timeline, at which the node first appears; 0 when absent. Added to the marker time when startMarker is set. A transition on the node can make it appear earlier.
                end: Time in seconds, on the parent's timeline, at which the node disappears (exclusive); when absent it stays until its parent ends. Added to the marker time when endMarker is set. A transition can keep it longer.
                shutterAngle: The shutter angle, in degrees, of this node's motion blur, instead of the project's: the nearest node up its parents that sets it, else project/@shutterAngle. 0 draws the node sharp; 360 blurs over the whole frame interval. Only where motion blur is on for the node.
                startMarker: Name of a scene marker, or a beat.N or bar.N id of the beat grid, whose time is added to start to give the node's appearance time.
                endMarker: Name of a scene marker, or a beat.N or bar.N id of the beat grid, whose time plus end (0 if absent) gives the node's disappearance time.
                condition: Node is rendered only when the expression is truthy (e.g. "param('showPrice')").
                motionBlur: Turns motion blur on or off for this node and the nodes it contains; inherit (the default) takes the nearest ancestor's setting, then the project's.
                matte: Track matte: any node whose alpha or luma gates this node. The matte node is not drawn itself unless matteVisible="true".
                matteMode: How the matte node gates this node: alpha or luma takes the matte's alpha or brightness as coverage, and the -inverted modes use one minus it; alpha when absent.
                matteVisible: On a node that names a matte: when true the matte node is also drawn; by default (false) the matte is hidden and only gates this node.
                edgeBlend: The space in which this node's own pixels (their colour C and coverage x opacity a) composite onto what lies beneath (B): linear, out = a C + (1 - a) B in the linear working space; encoded, the same on display-encoded values (the sRGB transfer function), decoded back; inherit, linear when project/@linearLight is true and encoded when it is false. A group's value applies when its offscreen composites; children do not inherit it. SREP 72.
                parent: Transform parent outside the XML tree (After Effects parenting); shorthand for a transformConstraint type="parent".
                threeD: 2.5D: place this 2D node in camera space at depth zDepth with rotationX/rotationY.
                zDepth: Depth of the node in the frame's 2.5D camera space, in frame pixels, used only when threeD is true; 0 when absent.
                rotationX: Rotation about the horizontal axis through the node's pivot, in degrees, used only when threeD is true; positive values turn the top edge away.
                rotationY: Rotation about the vertical axis through the node's pivot, in degrees, used only when threeD is true; positive values turn the right edge away.
                alignX: Responsive anchoring: overrides x so the node's box aligns within alignTo.
                alignY: Responsive vertical placement of the node's box within the alignTo rectangle: top, middle or bottom, or stretch to fill it minus margin; unset leaves y alone, as does a node with no box size.
                alignTo: Rectangle that alignX and alignY align within: the parent's box, the output frame, or the frame's safe area; parent when absent.
                margin: Inset in pixels or a relative length (a percentage is of the parent's width on both axes) kept from the alignTo edge for left, right, top, bottom and stretch alignment; 0 when absent, unused without alignX or alignY.
                x: Horizontal position of the node's anchor point in its parent's box, in pixels or a relative length (% of parent width, vw, vh, vmin, vmax); 0 when absent. alignX takes over on a node that has a box size.
                y: Vertical position of the node's anchor point in its parent's box, in pixels or a relative length (% of parent height, vw, vh, vmin, vmax), growing downward; 0 when absent. alignY takes over on a node that has a box size.
                rotation: Rotation about the anchor point, in degrees, clockwise on screen; 0 when absent.
                scaleX: Horizontal scale factor about the anchor point, applied before skew and rotation; 1 leaves the size unchanged and is used when absent.
                scaleY: Vertical scale factor about the anchor point, applied before skew and rotation; 1 leaves the size unchanged and is used when absent.
                anchorX: Horizontal pivot of the node's rotation, skew and scale, in the node's local layout coordinates (pixels or relative length, % of the parent's width); 0 when absent.
                anchorY: Vertical pivot of the node's rotation, skew and scale, in the node's local layout coordinates (pixels or relative length, % of the parent's height); 0 when absent.
                skewX: Horizontal shear angle in degrees (the tangent of the angle shifts x in proportion to y); 0 when absent.
                skewY: Vertical shear angle in degrees (the tangent of the angle shifts y in proportion to x); 0 when absent.
                steps: Number of steps each stateful node inside advances from its zero state before every frame is drawn (required); the ceiling when until is converged.
                until: steps (default) runs exactly steps steps; converged stops early once the state changes by no more than tolerance between two checks.
                tolerance: With until=converged, the largest per-channel change between two checks at or below which iteration stops (default 0.0001).
                checkEvery: With until=converged, the number of steps between convergence checks (default 100, at most steps).
                blend: Blend mode used to composite the iterate node's output over what lies below it (default normal).
            """
            ...

